        "surveyID": "110116",
        "narrative": "<p>LAKE TROUT ABUNDANCE WAS GOOD AND A WIDE RANGE OF AGE CLASSES WERE PRESENT. GROWTH WAS AVERAGE COOK COUNTY LAKES. NORTHERN CISCO ARE THE POPULATIONS ARE LOW. LAKE TROUT WERE PREYING ON YOY NORTHERN CISCO EXTENSIVELY DURING THIS SURVEY. SMALLMOUTH BASS ABUNDANCE WAS GOOD WITH A WIDE RANGE OF AGE CLASSES PRESENT. AGE V SMALLMOUTH BASS WERE NOT SAMPLED. SMALLMOUTH BASS GROWTH WAS SLOW WHICH IS TYPICAL OF MANY COOK COUNTY LAKES. WHITE SUCKER AND BURBOT WERE FAIRLY ABUNDANT. WHITE SUCKER LESS THEN 15 INCHES WERE RARE INDICA- TING A SENILE POPULATION. SIZE DISTRIBUTION OF BURBOT INCLUDED A WIDE RANGE OF LENGTHS FROM 13 TO 28 INCHES.</p>",
